<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I've solved the problem. I was trying to upgrade using Windows 11 under VMWare on my Mac. Finally gave up and borrowed a real Windows machine. All is well. As you guessed, the problem was the driver...didn't work under VMWare. Thanks again for a great project!!</div></blockquote>The problem is probably that W11 automatically installed the wrong version of driver.<br><br>The driver is from ST Micro who make the CPU.    Unfortunatly they released an updated driver last year, which is incompatible with existing firmware loaders.<br><br>I've no idea why they did something this stupid.  Possibly they didn't consider 3rd party firmware loaders.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Mon May 12, 2025 6:59 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
